u(\gamma_i)=0$. Let $T=T_1	imes T_2$ be the corresponding anisotropic torus of $G'$; explicitly we embed $T$ into $G$ as the subgroup $$ T=\left\{  mat{a &0 &\phantom{b}b\phantom{b}&\phantom{b}0\phantom{b}\ 0&c&0&d\ b\gamma_1\p &0&a&0\ 0&d\gamma_2\p & 0& c} \;\; \middle| \;\;\parbox{1.2in}{$a,b,c,d \in \R, \quad\quad$ $a^2-b^2\gamma_1\p = 1$, $c^2-d^2\gamma_2\p=1$}ight\}. $$ For each $i$, the point in the building $ uil(\SL_2,atk)$ corresponding to $T_i$ is the midpoint of the fundamental alcove. Thus the point $x$ representing $ uil(T)\subset  uil(G)$ is the midpoint of the diagonal facet $\F$ in the closure of the fundamental alcove $\C$ in the standard apartment $\apart$ of $ uil(G)$, as illustrated in Figure~ef{Fig:1}. Evidently $\overline{\F} \subseteq \apart^T$.  egin{figure}[ht]  egin{tikzpicture} \draw[fill=gray!20,ultra thick, gray!20] (1,1) rectangle (4,4); \draw (-4,1)--(9,1); \draw (-4,4)--(9,4); \draw (1,0)--(1,5); \draw (4,0)--(4,5); \draw (-2,0)--(-2,5); \draw (7,0)--(7,5); \draw (0,0)--(5,5); \draw (-3,5)--(2,0); \draw (3,5)--(8,0); \draw (6,0)--(9,3); \draw (-4,2)--(-1,5); \draw[fill] (2.5,2.5) circle [radius=2pt]; 
