eq \overline{\F}$. Let $y$ denote the (non-special) vertex of $\overline{\C}$ opposite $\F$, and $w\in G$ a reflection in the wall of $\apart$ containing $\F$ (viewed as a representative of the corresponding element of the affine Weyl group). Adopting the convention that a matrix ring stands for its intersection with $\Sp_4(atk)$, we compute directly that  egin{equation} G_{\C} =  mat{\R & \R & \R & \R \ \PP & \R & \R&\R \ \PP &\PP & \R&\PP\ \PP&\PP&\R&\R} \quad 	ext{and} \quad G_{w\C} =  mat{\R & \PP & \R & \R \ \R & \R & \R&\R \ \PP &\PP & \R&\R\ \PP&\PP&\PP&\R}, \end{equation} each of which contains $T$ as a subgroup. It therefore follows that $\{y,wy\} \subset \overline{\C}\cup \overline{w\C}\subseteq \apart^T$, even though neither $y$ nor $wy$ lie in $\overline{\F}$. Applying now Lemma~ef{L:strongunicityfails}, we deduce that strong unicity fails for any supercuspidal representation $\pi(\Psi)$ constructed from $G^0=T$.
